  "slug": "doubling-genome-bb89",
  "summary": "A 41,332-tumour pan-cancer analysis now dates whole-genome doubling against drivers, chromosomal losses and immune programmes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is evolutionary timing of whole-genome doubling (WGD) in human cancer. A pan-cancer analysis of 41,332 tumours across 12 cancer types dates WGD relative to driver events, chromosomal losses and immune programmes, which is the new element here. A related preprint maps mosaic chromosomal alterations across 19 tissues from 722 WGS samples, reporting tissue-specific mitotic error and purifying selection; it concerns non-tumour tissue and is not doubling-specific. The remaining items are plant and subgenome studies: UMR-seq for combined epigenetic and genetic variation, vafSOMA for cell-layer-fixed somatic mutations, and explainable machine learning on recombination and chromatin context in maize and Brassica. They do not address WGD.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-07"
}
